    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d513">

                <pb facs="0595" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg502"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">339.115 General Motors Export Co./159:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-20T19:00:00-04:00">May 20, 1935—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>28. Your 71 May 20, 1 p.m.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d513-f1"/> You are authorized to
                    urge President Trujillo to withdraw charges against Barletta, making appropriate
                        <pb facs="0596" n="503" xml:id="pg503"/> reference to my statements to the
                    Dominican Minister as reported in Department’s 25 May 14, 7 p.m. and to the fact
                    that American interests are sustaining injury as the result of Barletta’s
                    continued imprisonment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
